    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "What is Australia's 5,614 kilometre fence keeping out?",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.73,
        "window": 4.33,
        "fill": 0.861
      },
      {
        "scene": "cliffs",
        "text": "It starts on the cliffs of the south coast: wire 180 centimetres high, taller than you.",
        "start": 4.63,
        "seconds": 4.07,
        "window": 4.73,
        "fill": 0.86
      },
      {
        "scene": "north",
        "text": "From there it runs north, across the red dunes and salt pans of the South Australian desert.",
        "start": 9.37,
        "seconds": 4.18,
        "window": 4.77,
        "fill": 0.876
      },
      {
        "scene": "east",
        "text": "Then it swings east to the corner where three states meet, crosses into New South Wales, and climbs north through Queensland,",
        "start": 14.13,
        "seconds": 4.95,
        "window": 5.6,
        "fill": 0.884
      },
      {
        "scene": "farms",
        "text": "until it finally stops among the farms of the Darling Downs.",
        "start": 19.73,
        "seconds": 2.69,
        "window": 3.37,
        "fill": 0.798
      },
      {
        "scene": "split",
        "text": "Now look at the map again. One wire splits the land into two sides. So what lives on each side of it?",
        "start": 23.1,
        "seconds": 4.31,
        "window": 4.93,
        "fill": 0.874
      },
      {
        "scene": "sheep",
        "text": "To the south and east is sheep country: flock after flock, grazing on open grass.",
        "start": 28.03,
        "seconds": 3.76,
        "window": 4.43,
        "fill": 0.849
      },
      {
        "scene": "rabbits",
        "text": "It began in the eighteen-eighties as a fence against rabbits, and against rabbits it failed. So why keep it?",
        "start": 32.47,
        "seconds": 4.44,
        "window": 5.07,
        "fill": 0.876
      },
      {
        "scene": "dingo",
        "text": "Because on the other side lives the hunter of sheep: the dingo, Australia's wild dog, roaming the north and west.",
        "start": 37.53,
        "seconds": 4.92,
        "window": 5.57,
        "fill": 0.883
      },
      {
        "scene": "built",
        "text": "So the wire was raised and joined into one fence, post by post, kilometre after kilometre, to keep the dingo out.",
        "start": 43.1,
        "seconds": 5.45,
        "window": 6.1,
        "fill": 0.893
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "And it used to be even longer: over 8,000 kilometres of wire, all to stop one hungry wild dog.",
        "start": 49.2,
        "seconds": 4.7,
        "window": 5.33,
        "fill": 0.882
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "Sheep side or dingo side: which would you pick? Now you know what one wire across Australia is keeping out.",
        "start": 54.53,
        "seconds": 4.73,
        "window": 5.33,
        "fill": 0.887
      }
    ]
  },
